{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02841",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.77,
      "end_seconds": 5.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "right, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.24,
      "end_seconds": 11.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.22,
      "end_seconds": 18.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.1,
      "end_seconds": 23.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 25.94,
      "end_seconds": 29.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "we came because of sneezing in spring"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.58,
      "end_seconds": 34.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 36.51,
      "end_seconds": 43.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "She is on loratadine, 10 milligrams, once a day, I give it it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.91,
      "end_seconds": 53.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.3,
      "end_seconds": 57.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "I'd say a week, maybe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 58.27,
      "end_seconds": 62.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "right, hm, I'd say more like two weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.18,
      "end_seconds": 71.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.01,
      "end_seconds": 75.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Mm, yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.08,
      "end_seconds": 81.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "okay, rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.88,
      "end_seconds": 83.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Mild, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.73,
      "end_seconds": 88.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "So, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.14,
      "end_seconds": 101.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "A runny itchy nose goes along with it, most of the time let me think, and there's watery eyes as well, three days now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.57,
      "end_seconds": 106.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "have you had fever, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.33,
      "end_seconds": 112.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "No fever, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 114.4,
      "end_seconds": 120.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.11,
      "end_seconds": 127.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "no, I don't think I did maybe a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.49,
      "end_seconds": 138.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Did you get loss of smell, wheeze or facial pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.93,
      "end_seconds": 141.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.01,
      "end_seconds": 148.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.16,
      "end_seconds": 153.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.06,
      "end_seconds": 159.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.32,
      "end_seconds": 164.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Hmm, bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.29,
      "end_seconds": 167.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.33,
      "end_seconds": 171.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Eczema, for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.62,
      "end_seconds": 179.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "alright, eczema, that matches what I have here. Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.89,
      "end_seconds": 186.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.26,
      "end_seconds": 191.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.63,
      "end_seconds": 194.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.02,
      "end_seconds": 199.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.18,
      "end_seconds": 205.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.92,
      "end_seconds": 209.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.13,
      "end_seconds": 214.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Just my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.12,
      "end_seconds": 219.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.82,
      "end_seconds": 222.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.89,
      "end_seconds": 226.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.27,
      "end_seconds": 239.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, uh, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 256.73,
      "end_seconds": 265.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pulse is 80 beats a minute, BP is 124 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.16,
      "end_seconds": 267.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.99,
      "end_seconds": 274.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.57,
      "end_seconds": 279.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.28,
      "end_seconds": 282.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.74,
      "end_seconds": 299.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "The inside of the nose is pale and boggy with clear mucus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.09,
      "end_seconds": 301.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.8,
      "end_seconds": 313.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Right, here's what I'm thinking. My working impression is seasonal allergic rhinitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.19,
      "end_seconds": 342.44,
      "duration_seconds": 21.25,
      "text": "the treatment will be fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, the season. That should help with hay fever. Shower after being outdoors and keep windows shut when pollen is high. Let's plan a check if not better in a month. I think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.93,
      "end_seconds": 347.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Oh, um, alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.68,
      "end_seconds": 350.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "have a good day"
    }
  ]
}